# jq.test programs (by line) where deem prints something other than plain
# jaq, and why: only where deem differs from jaq on purpose.
1601	import: deem refuses a program that loads files (plain jaq here has no loader and crashes)
1618	module: deem's directive is an object with input and defaults; jaq takes any term
1622	module: as 1618
2002	fromjson, and tonumber built on it, read exactly one value: jaq reads "2a" as 2, and loops on some invalid text
